WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
Marcus let an ordinary individual life policy lapse after its premium

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:08.020
grace period. Reinstatement may restore that policy when the required

3
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:12.520
conditions are satisfied. Maryland's standard provision allows an application

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.520
within three years from the due date of the first premium

5
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.900
in default. It requires a written application, satisfactory evidence of

6
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:26.040
insurability, overdue premiums, and payment or reinstatement of other policy

7
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.680
debt with the allowed interest.

8
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.360
It does not apply when the policy was surrendered for cash,

9
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:35.680
its cash value was exhausted by debt, or paid-up term coverage

10
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.340
has expired. Check eligibility before promising that a late payment alone

11
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:45.070
restores insurance. Suppose Marcus applies within the permitted period but

12
00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.590
gives an inaccurate answer about a health change material to reinstatement.

13
00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:55.130
Maryland permits a contest of a reinstated life policy for fraud

14
00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:59.870
or misrepresentation material to that reinstatement, under the same period,

15
00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:04.630
conditions and exceptions that apply after original issue.

16
00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:08.800
The period is measured after reinstatement.

17
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.090
This is different from treating every old statement as newly contestable

18
00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:15.550
without examining what the statute permits.

19
00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:20.890
Industrial life also has a different standard reinstatement window of two

20
00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:26.330
years. Keep the policy category, first default date, reinstatement date

21
00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.670
and actual disputed statement on a clear timeline.

22
00:01:30.732 --> 00:01:34.592
An age correction ordinarily adjusts the benefit to what the premium

23
00:01:34.592 --> 00:01:37.992
would have purchased at the correct age under Maryland's standard provision.

24
00:01:38.892 --> 00:01:42.945
Assume a teaching policy states one hundred thousand dollars, with two

25
00:01:42.945 --> 00:01:45.532
hundred dollars paid for the relevant premium period.

26
00:01:46.332 --> 00:01:50.892
The correct-age premium for that same stated
coverage would have been two hundred fifty dollars.

28
00:01:51.572 --> 00:01:55.465
Under the stated proportional formula, two hundred divided by two hundred

29
00:01:55.465 --> 00:01:57.772
fifty equals eighty percent.

30
00:01:57.772 --> 00:02:00.612
The adjusted benefit is eighty thousand dollars.

31
00:02:01.372 --> 00:02:05.592
Actual policy formulas and statutory age-limit exceptions matter.

32
00:02:06.212 --> 00:02:10.152
Where a contract also adjusts for misstated sex, use its lawful

33
00:02:10.152 --> 00:02:11.772
rate and adjustment provision.

34
00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:17.450
A suicide exclusion is separate from an incontestability provision.

35
00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:23.270
Maryland permits the stated individual-life exclusion for suicide, whether

36
00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:28.570
sane or insane, within two years from issue, subject to

37
00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:33.390
its special continuity rules when the same insurer replaces earlier coverage.

38
00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:38.630
Do not assume every new policy automatically restarts the full period

39
00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.870
for all previously insured benefits.

40
00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:45.730
The contract and statute also determine the amount payable when an

41
00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:50.450
allowed exclusion applies. Maryland sets a minimum tied to the policy's

42
00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:53.470
statutory reserve and specified adjustments.

43
00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:57.650
A more favorable policy may promise a premium refund.

44
00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:03.050
Read that actual promise instead of calling every excluded claim a

45
00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:07.704
zero payment. Maryland allows particular war

46
00:03:08.084 --> 00:03:12.564
or military-service restrictions and other specified exclusions.

47
00:03:12.944 --> 00:03:17.564
Read whether a policy uses a status-based restriction or one tied

48
00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.844
to the cause of death.

49
00:03:19.864 --> 00:03:23.544
A statement about military membership is different from a statement about

50
00:03:23.544 --> 00:03:24.944
death caused by war.

51
00:03:25.824 --> 00:03:30.584
The statute also addresses aviation, specified hazardous work or recreation,

52
00:03:31.184 --> 00:03:34.424
and certain residence conditions, with different limits.

53
00:03:35.484 --> 00:03:39.644
It prohibits excluding death from terrorism when the insured was a

54
00:03:39.644 --> 00:03:41.344
victim who did not participate.

55
00:03:42.304 --> 00:03:46.064
A producer must explain the actual policy restriction accurately.

56
00:03:47.064 --> 00:03:50.824
A general claim that every life policy excludes every military death

57
00:03:50.824 --> 00:03:55.906
would be wrong. Maryland prohibits knowingly issuing

58
00:03:55.906 --> 00:04:01.146
premium-saving life insurance more than six months before the actual

59
00:04:01.146 --> 00:04:05.046
application date under the statutory conditions.

60
00:04:06.306 --> 00:04:10.566
It separately prohibits a producer from falsely dating the application

61
00:04:10.566 --> 00:04:14.206
earlier to obtain that lower age-based premium.

62
00:04:15.226 --> 00:04:19.706
Limited permitted policy backdating does not authorize changing when the

63
00:04:19.706 --> 00:04:24.200
client actually applied. Other prohibited provisions also

64
00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:30.386
matter. For example, a policy cannot reduce its benefit merely because

65
00:04:30.386 --> 00:04:34.246
the same insurer issued another policy on that life.

66
00:04:34.926 --> 00:04:39.686
Some medical-history or prior-rejection provisions have specific statutory

67
00:04:39.686 --> 00:04:43.686
limits rather than unrestricted cancellation power.

68
00:04:44.186 --> 00:04:49.086
Record the true facts, read the lawful contract, and identify the

69
00:04:49.086 --> 00:04:50.266
exact rule involved.
